    <item>
      <title>Avoid using &lt;object&gt; tag inside anchor &lt;a&gt; tag</title>
      <link>https://sanjeevkpandit.github.io/posts/avoid-using-object-tag-inside-anchor-tag/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sanjeevkpandit.github.io/posts/avoid-using-object-tag-inside-anchor-tag/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I have been recently working on a project where I got an issue with the anchor&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/a&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tag. The issue was with the hover effect on the&#xA;anchor tag. There was no hover effect over the link. Plus, the link was not working either. However,&#xA;the hover effect was seen below the link for small space. The anchor element had a&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/object&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;object&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; element inside it and that was the&#xA;reason of the issue. The link element looked like this:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
